BUG: /dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js is:

  export default (o, c) => {
    const proto = c.prototype
    proto.weekYear = function () {
      const month = this.month()
      const weekOfYear = this.week()
      const year = this.year()
      if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
        return year + 1
      }
      return year
    }
  }

It is missing the symmetric case: when the date is in January (month === 0) and its ISO week number is >= 52 (i.e. it belongs to the last week of the previous year, which happens with locales that set `yearStart: 4`, e.g. en-gb/fr/zh-cn), weekYear must return `year - 1`.

FIX: insert before `return year`:

      if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
        return year - 1
      }

(keep 2-space indentation, keep the existing `weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11` branch).

