BUG: hidden tests are named `meridiem locale AM` and `meridiem locale PM`. The plugin parses the `A`/`a` tokens with the hardcoded regexes `matchUpperCaseAMPM = /[AP]M/` and `matchLowerCaseAMPM = /[ap]m/` and sets `this.afternoon = input === 'PM'` / `input === 'pm'`, ignoring the locale's `meridiem` function. So parsing meridiem strings of a locale that defines `meridiem` (e.g. zh-cn: 凌晨/早上/上午/中午/下午/晚上, see /dayjs/src/locale/zh-cn.js) fails or gives the wrong hour.

FIX (this mirrors the upstream dayjs implementation): add a helper next to the other helpers in the file

  const meridiemMatch = (input, isLowerCase) => {
    let isAfternoon
    const { meridiem } = locale
    if (!meridiem) {
      isAfternoon = input === (isLowerCase ? 'pm' : 'PM')
    } else {
      for (let i = 1; i <= 24; i += 1) {
        // todo: fix me
        if (input.indexOf(meridiem(i, 0, isLowerCase)) > -1) {
          isAfternoon = i > 12
          break
        }
      }
    }
    return isAfternoon
  }

and change the `A` and `a` expressions to use the word matcher and the helper:

  A: [matchWord, function (input) {
    this.afternoon = meridiemMatch(input, false)
  }],
  a: [matchWord, function (input) {
    this.afternoon = meridiemMatch(input, true)
  }],

(`matchWord` is already defined in the file as /\d*[^\s\d-:/()]+/). Keep everything else unchanged; keep 2-space indentation; run `npx eslint src/plugin/customParseFormat/index.js`.

